From 15b15c0e2a140b129a0409e75e6303736f78dfa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 23:35:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] Split live tracker into sessions + subagents
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User feedback: the live tracker increments when a Task(background=true)
spawns its child session — turns out this is exactly what users want
(visibility into running subagents) IF the count is split out from the
parent-session count. Otherwise "● 4 live" with one TUI attached looks
broken.

This patch records `parentID` at SSE subscription time. A session is
classified as a subagent iff `parentID != null`. The classification is
immutable for the life of the subscription (a session's parent doesn't
change).

LiveSessionsChanged payload extended:
  { sessions: string[], subagents: string[] }

`sessions` remains the full live set; `subagents` is the subset whose
parent is set. Existing consumers that only read `sessions` still work.
TUI footer (next patch) consumes both, computes
`roots = sessions.length - subagents.length`, and shows two pills
("N sessions", "N subagents").

`/global/live-sessions` returns the same shape. Lookup happens in the
SSE request handler before entering streamSSE — one Session.get per
subscription, no DB load on per-event publishes.

Lookup failures (session not found, transient DB issue) treat the
session as a root rather than failing the SSE subscription. Slight
miscount is preferable to a broken stream.
